## First run

Generation does no network work and runs no tools, so these are the exact
commands to run once, in order, from this directory:

```sh
go mod edit -replace {{.NiseModule}}={{.ReplacePlaceholder}}  # temporary; see above
go mod tidy                      # resolve and record the Go dependencies
pnpm --dir frontend install      # resolve the frontend dependencies
pnpm --dir frontend build        # build the frontend into the Go package
nise dev                         # start PostgreSQL, Go, and Vite
```

Then open <http://127.0.0.1:8080>. To run the application binary directly,
set `DATABASE_URL`; the application does not load `.env` files.

`go build ./cmd/... ./db/... ./internal/...` also works before the frontend has ever
been built: a placeholder page is committed inside the embedding Go package
for exactly that reason, and the server serves it in development. In
production a missing frontend build is a startup failure, not a placeholder.

Commit `go.sum` and `frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml` after the first run.

